description:
In `fragmentation_vectors.rs`, the packet_sha256 verification was changed from:
```
let digest = Sha256::digest(expand(packet));
let expected = decode_hex(vector.packet_sha256.as_ref().unwrap());
assert_eq!(&digest[..], expected);
```
to:
```
if vector.packet.is_some() {
    assert!(vector.packet_sha256.is_some());
}
```

The new code only checks that the field exists, not that it matches the computed hash. The `use sha2::{Digest, Sha256}` import was removed. This weakens test coverage by silently accepting incorrect hash values.
